---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Bundled language model
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

The files under `buttcrack/data/` are a derived statistical model of English,
built by `scripts/build_language_model.py`. They are not source code and not
secret material: they are letter n-gram counts and a word-frequency dictionary
used to judge whether a candidate decryption reads as English.

The model is derived from two openly licensed upstream sources, both fetched
from PyPI at build time:

  * wordsegment 1.3.1 -- Apache License 2.0
    Supplies the unigram and bigram frequency lists originally compiled by
    Peter Norvig from the Google Web 1T corpus (1/ngram, "Web 1T corpus",
    distributed by the LDC). buttcrack uses the derived frequency tables, not
    the library itself.
      https://pypi.org/project/wordsegment/

  * pyspellchecker 0.9.0 -- MIT License
    Supplies the English word-frequency dictionary from which the 80,000 most
    common words were taken.
      https://pypi.org/project/pyspellchecker/

`buttcrack/data/model_meta.json` records the exact versions, the sampling seed,
the corpus size (25,000,000 words) and the resulting table sizes, so a build is
reproducible and the provenance travels with the data.

Neither upstream project endorses this one. The Apache-2.0 and MIT notices above
are reproduced in summary form; the full license texts are available from the
respective project pages.

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party runtime dependencies
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

None. buttcrack uses only the Python standard library at runtime.
